cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this threat model or dataset, please cite it as below."
title: "AI Security Atlas: an interactive threat-to-guardrail map for AI agents, LLM applications, and RAG"
abstract: >-
  An open, interactive threat model linking adversarial threats against AI agents,
  LLM applications, and retrieval-augmented generation to the vulnerabilities they
  exploit and to concrete guardrails, with remediation and verification steps.
  Entries are mapped to the OWASP Top 10 for LLM Applications (2025), the OWASP
  Top 10 for Agentic Applications (2026), MITRE ATLAS, and the NIST AI RMF.
  Independent project; not affiliated with MITRE.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ngo
    given-names: Clark
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-10-07
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/clarkngo/ai-sec-atlas"
url: "https://clarkngo.github.io/ai-sec-atlas/"
keywords:
